# Agent Rita on the Spark — deploy as /home/dev/rita/rita.env (chmod 600).
# Real values NEVER enter git.
#
# The model servers are vLLM containers on the SAME host (see "Model host" in
# README.md). Both they and Rita run `--network host`, so Rita reaches them on
# loopback — the old `<SPARK_TS_IP>` indirection is no longer needed.
#
#   <MODEL_PORT>  8000 = `qwen`  → qwen3-14b     (role: coding/agent)
#                 8001 = `gemma` → gemma-4-26b   (role: general)
#   <MODEL_ID>    curl -s http://127.0.0.1:<MODEL_PORT>/v1/models | jq -r '.data[0].id'
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY is a non-empty placeholder, NOT a secret: the vLLM servers run
# without `--api-key`, but the OpenAI SDK refuses to construct a client with an
# empty key. This replaces the llama.cpp era's per-consumer key file
# (`/root/keys/qwen.keys`, `SPARK_KEY_RITA`), which no longer exists.
#
# Rita takes ONE OPENAI_BASE_URL, so it can reach exactly one of the two
# servers. DEFAULT_MODEL must name the model THAT server serves — every other
# id in agents.json's model picker fails with
# `Model error: The model \`X\` does not exist.`
OPENAI_API_KEY=local-only
OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
DEFAULT_MODEL=openai:qwen3-14b
PORT=8002
